\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa220\sl276\slmult1\f0\fs24\b FarmConnect Project Report\b0\par
\pard\sa180\sl260\slmult1 Generated from the current codebase state.\par
\par
\b 1. Project Overview\b0\par
FarmConnect is a cross-platform mobile application for Android and iOS built as a social-media-inspired agriculture platform with marketplace features. The product combines a feed-first experience, a marketplace for farm products and inputs, community discussions, user profiles, onboarding, media uploads, notifications, trust scoring, and a growing order flow.\par
\par
The repository is structured as a monorepo with:\par
- a mobile client in client/mobile built with Expo and React Native\par
- a backend API in server built with Node.js, Express, and MongoDB\par
\par
\b 2. Current Product Vision Implemented So Far\b0\par
- Animated launch and onboarding flow\par
- Feed-first home screen inspired by modern social apps\par
- Marketplace listings with seller details and product detail pages\par
- Community discussions with thread detail and replies\par
- Profile pages with avatar editing, follower graphs, public profile views, and notifications\par
- Auth flow with sign up, login, demo login, and guest mode\par
- Logout flow with a choice to fully log out or continue browsing as guest\par
- Media upload support for images and videos using Cloudinary\par
- Comment, like, save, follow, reply, and notification systems\par
- Dynamic trust score and verification status logic\par
- Initial order flow from product details into the Orders tab\par
- Feed and post-detail media playback with resume state, off-screen pause behavior, and full-post viewing\par
- Settings screen for privacy, account actions, activity review, and logout flow\par
\par
\b 3. Repository Structure\b0\par
\b Root\b0\par
- package.json\par
- .env at the project root for shared environment configuration\par
- FarmConnect_Project_Report.rtf\par
\par
\b Server folders\b0\par
- server/config: environment, database, Cloudinary configuration\par
- server/controllers: route logic for auth, feed, comments, marketplace, profile, community, and orders\par
- server/data: seed script for demo data\par
- server/middleware: auth and upload middleware\par
- server/models: MongoDB schemas for users, posts, orders, notifications, replies, products, and related entities\par
- server/routes: Express routers\par
- server/scripts: utility scripts such as trust score recalculation\par
- server/utils: shared helpers such as trust score, media upload, JWT, errors, and notifications\par
\par
\b Client mobile app routes\b0\par
- app/index.tsx: animated launch screen\par
- app/get-started.tsx: get started screen with sign up, login, Google placeholder, phone placeholder, guest path\par
- app/auth.tsx: login and registration flow\par
- app/modal.tsx: create post and create listing composer\par
- app/onboarding.tsx: onboarding support screen\par
- app/(tabs)/index.tsx: feed screen\par
- app/(tabs)/marketplace.tsx: marketplace overview\par
- app/(tabs)/community.tsx: community overview\par
- app/(tabs)/orders.tsx: orders and sales screen\par
- app/(tabs)/profile.tsx: profile and notifications\par
- app/post/[id].tsx: full post detail screen with comments and expanded media\par
- app/profile/[id].tsx: public profile screen for other users\par
- app/settings.tsx: settings, privacy, activity, and logout screen\par
- app/community/new.tsx: create discussion thread\par
- app/community/[id].tsx: thread detail and replies\par
- app/product/[id].tsx: product details and checkout flow\par
\par
\b 4. Client-Side Components and Responsibilities\b0\par
\b Navigation and app shell\b0\par
- Expo Router is used for route-based mobile navigation.\par
- The root layout handles splash behavior, theming, and stack registration.\par
- Bottom tabs organize the main app into Feed, Marketplace, Community, Orders, and Profile.\par
\par
\b Session and auth state\b0\par
- SessionProvider stores token, user data, mode, and intro state.\par
- Modes supported: signed-out, guest, authenticated.\par
- Session restore runs on app launch.\par
- Logout supports two paths: full logout to login screen or switch to guest browsing.\par
\par
\b Feed\b0\par
- Displays posts with author avatar, engagement data, media, and recent comments.\par
- Supports filtering, comments, likes, saves, follow actions, and author profile navigation.\par
- Supports image and video rendering in feed posts, including multi-media posts.\par
- Supports full post detail viewing for long-form content and expanded media.\par
- Feed videos pause off-screen and preserve playback position when the user scrolls away and back.\par
\par
\b Marketplace\b0\par
- Lists products from sellers with lighter browsing chrome and cleaner filter presentation.\par
- Product detail now supports quantity selection, delivery details, and order placement.\par
\par
\b Community\b0\par
- Shows discussion threads by category.\par
- Supports opening a thread, viewing replies, and posting a reply.\par
- Supports creating new community threads.\par
- Uses a lighter discussion-first header rather than heavy dashboard blocks.\par
\par
\b Orders\b0\par
- Shows buyer purchases and seller-side sales.\par
- Refreshes on screen focus.\par
- Displays status, ETA, amount, item summary, and delivery location where available.\par
\par
\b Profile\b0\par
- Shows user avatar, role, bio, metrics, trust score, verification status, and notifications.\par
- Supports editing avatar and profile fields.\par
- Supports notification read state and mark-all-read behavior.\par
- Supports profile tabs for posts, listings, followers, and following.\par
- Supports public profile browsing and follow/unfollow behavior across the app.\par
\par
\b Settings\b0\par
- Provides an account-management entry point from profile.\par
- Includes account, privacy, activity, and logout actions.\par
- Supports logout with a guest-browsing fallback path.\par
\par
\b Composer\b0\par
- The modal composer supports both feed posts and marketplace listings.\par
- Allows media selection for photos and videos.\par
- Shows staged upload feedback and validation messaging.\par
\par
\b 5. Server-Side Components and Responsibilities\b0\par
\b Config\b0\par
- env.js validates required environment variables.\par
- db.js connects to MongoDB.\par
- cloudinary.js configures Cloudinary uploads.\par
\par
\b Middleware\b0\par
- auth.middleware.js handles optional auth, required auth, and role checks.\par
- upload.middleware.js handles multipart uploads.\par
\par
\b Models\b0\par
- User: account data, profile fields, trust score, verification status\par
- Post: feed posts and attached media\par
- Comment: feed comments\par
- SavedPost: saved-feed relation\par
- LikedPost: liked-feed relation\par
- Product: marketplace listing\par
- Order: buyer-seller transaction\par
- Notification: social and marketplace notifications\par
- CommunityThread: discussion thread\par
- ThreadReply: replies to discussion threads\par
\par
\b Controllers\b0\par
- auth.controller.js: registration, login, session retrieval\par
- feed.controller.js: feed retrieval, filtering, post creation, follow-state shaping, and post deletion\par
- comments.controller.js: feed comments, save toggles, like toggles\par
- marketplace.controller.js: marketplace overview, product list, product detail, product creation\par
- community.controller.js: thread list, thread detail, thread creation, reply creation, reply retrieval\par
- orders.controller.js: order creation and order retrieval\par
- profile.controller.js: own profile retrieval, public profile retrieval, update, and notification read actions\par
\par
\b Utilities\b0\par
- trust-score.js: dynamic trust score and verification recalculation\par
- notifications.js: notification creation helper\par
- media-upload.js: Cloudinary media upload helpers\par
- jwt.js: token creation\par
- app-error.js and async-handler.js: error handling utilities\par
\par
\b 6. Current User Flow\b0\par
\b App launch\b0\par
1. User taps the FarmConnect app icon.\par
2. Animated splash screen appears with FarmConnect branding.\par
3. The app checks session state and whether intro has been seen.\par
\par
\b If the user is already authenticated\b0\par
1. The app restores the session.\par
2. The user is taken directly to the main tab flow.\par
3. Default experience centers around the feed screen.\par
\par
\b If the user is in guest mode\b0\par
1. The app restores guest mode.\par
2. The user goes straight into browse-only access.\par
3. Interactive account-bound features remain restricted.\par
\par
\b If the user is new\b0\par
1. The app opens the Get Started screen.\par
2. The user can choose Create account, Log in, Continue with Google placeholder, Continue with phone placeholder, or Continue as guest.\par
\par
\b Sign up flow\b0\par
1. User chooses a role: farmer, buyer, or hobbyist.\par
2. User selects interests.\par
3. User may upload an optional profile photo.\par
4. User enters name, email, password, and location.\par
5. Password is hashed on the server before storage.\par
6. Session is created and the user enters the app.\par
\par
\b Login flow\b0\par
1. User enters email and password.\par
2. Credentials are verified by the backend.\par
3. JWT session is returned.\par
4. User enters the app.\par
\par
\b Guest flow\b0\par
1. User chooses Continue as guest.\par
2. User enters the app without authenticated account privileges.\par
3. Browse-only experiences are available.\par
\par
\b Feed flow\b0\par
1. User opens feed.\par
2. Feed displays posts, social content, sponsored content, and media.\par
3. User can like, comment, save, follow authors, and open author profiles if authenticated.\par
4. User can open long-form posts into a dedicated detail screen.\par
5. Videos pause when off-screen or when the app backgrounds, and resume from their saved playback position.\par
\par
\b Marketplace to order flow\b0\par
1. User opens a product in the marketplace.\par
2. User reviews seller trust and product detail.\par
3. User sets quantity, delivery location, contact, and note.\par
4. User places an order.\par
5. Stock is reduced on the backend.\par
6. Buyer and seller notifications are created.\par
7. Order appears in Orders tab.\par
\par
\b Logout and account switching flow\b0\par
1. User taps Log out from profile.\par
2. App asks whether to continue browsing as guest or fully log out.\par
3. User can switch quickly to another account afterward.\par
\par
\b Profile and social graph flow\b0\par
1. User taps an author from the feed or comments.\par
2. App opens a public profile page showing posts, listings, followers, and following.\par
3. User can follow or unfollow that account from the public profile or feed context.\par
4. Owners manage their own profile and settings from the profile tab.\par
\par
\b 7. Trust Score Feature Summary\b0\par
The trust score is now dynamic instead of being purely decorative.\par
\par
\b Inputs currently influencing trust score\b0\par
- avatar present\par
- bio present\par
- phone present\par
- location present\par
- interests present\par
- number of posts\par
- number of community threads\par
- number of comments\par
- number of listings for sellers\par
- number of buyer orders\par
- number of seller orders\par
- number of delivered sales\par
\par
\b Verification status logic\b0\par
- Farmers can become unverified, verified, or top-rated based on trust score and delivered sales.\par
- Non-farmer accounts can move between unverified and verified based on trust score and profile strength.\par
\par
\b Recalculation triggers\b0\par
- register user\par
- update profile\par
- create feed post\par
- create marketplace listing\par
- create comment\par
- create community thread\par
- create community reply\par
- create order\par
\par
\b 8. Order Flow Summary\b0\par
\b Backend behavior\b0\par
- validates product and quantity\par
- blocks self-ordering\par
- blocks orders larger than available stock\par
- reduces product stock when order is placed\par
- stores note, delivery location, and delivery contact\par
- creates notifications for buyer and seller\par
- updates trust score for both sides\par
\par
\b Mobile behavior\b0\par
- product screen supports quantity stepper\par
- supports delivery details and note\par
- places order through authenticated API call\par
- redirects user to Orders screen after success\par
- Orders tab supports buyer and seller views\par
\par
\b 9. Notifications Implemented\b0\par
- new comment on a post\par
- new like on a post\par
- new reply on a community thread\par
- new marketplace order\par
- buyer confirmation when order is placed\par
- read/unread tracking\par
- mark one notification as read\par
- mark all notifications as read\par
\par
\b 10. Authentication Status\b0\par
\b Implemented now\b0\par
- email and password registration\par
- hashed passwords using bcryptjs\par
- email and password login\par
- JWT-based mobile session\par
- guest browsing mode\par
- demo buyer login\par
- logout to sign-in screen\par
- logout to guest mode\par
- session restore and route-based jump into the main app experience\par
\par
\b Planned but not yet fully implemented\b0\par
- Google login\par
- phone OTP login\par
- other social login providers\par
