\par
\b 14. What Is Working Well Right Now\b0\par
- Mobile navigation and session flow are stable\par
- Feed, community, marketplace, notifications, profile, and settings feel connected\par
- Media uploads are supported\par
- Public profile browsing, following, and richer social context are now in place\par
- Feed media behavior is more controlled, with off-screen pausing and expanded post viewing\par
- Trust score now reflects user activity more realistically\par
- Order flow has started moving from browsing into actual transaction state\par
- Guest mode and account switching are now easier to use\par
\par
\b 15. Recommended Next Steps\b0\par
- Build Google authentication end to end\par
- Add phone OTP login\par
- Add order status update actions for sellers and buyers\par
- Add tap-through notification navigation to related post/thread/order\par
- Wire compact search and filter actions into real search/filter sheets and backend filtering\par
- Add richer video controls and composition options such as crop/trim before upload\par
- Add stronger admin or moderation tools for verification and disputes\par
- Add push notifications later once core auth providers are in place\par
\par
\b 16. Final Summary\b0\par
FarmConnect already has the foundations of a strong social-commerce agriculture app. The client side now covers onboarding, authentication, guest mode, social feed, marketplace, community threads, replies, public and private profiles, follow relationships, settings, notifications, and early checkout. The server side already supports real authentication, media upload, MongoDB persistence, Cloudinary integration, social engagement, notifications, trust scoring, and early order processing.\par
\par
The codebase is no longer just a visual prototype. It is now an early working product foundation with clear next steps toward production-grade auth, ordering, and marketplace trust.\par
